name:Ostende nobis (Asperges, versicles, Paschaltide);
office-part:Versus;
book:Missale O.P. (1939), p. 33 ("Postea dicat Sacerdos ... Temp. Pasch. Allelúia"), text; set to the Dominican tone of the versicles "quotiescumque dicitur V. a Sacerdote", Processionarium O.P. (1913), pp. 395-396 (Art. II, IV 3°), with allelúia as in the example "Dícite in natiónibus, allelúia", p. 396;
transcriber:set to the printed tone (F clef on the 3rd line, reciting note h; the syllables after the last accent on f);
